@@ -0,0 +1,21 @@
+# Durable native submission prototype
+
+`submission_submit` binds a permanent client identity to the exact protected native target, immutable preparation identity and input bytes. A reservation is published before extension, builtin, abort, model or tool dispatch. Duplicate keys return existing facts without executing. Conflicting bytes or targets are refused. This does not promise exactly-once external effects: a crashed reserved input remains unresolved and never resumes automatically.
+
+`submission_query` reads the protected logical native bytes without executing, flushing, repairing or retrying. A reservation differs from completion; individual committed entry relations differ from memory observations, explicit no-entry decisions and unresolved outcomes. Durable means recoverability after a software process crash, not fsync or power-loss durability. The native control ledger admits at most 10,000 permanent keys / 32 MiB; full ledgers refuse new admission, never evict tombstones. Query pages have at most 128 relations. The ledger stays outside the 16 KiB catalog prefix and outside the native tree/model index. After one protected feature upgrade, reservation and completion append verified control records instead of rewriting the full history. Native entries hold minimal causal origin fields; metadata contains no prompt copy. Reservation/completion preserve the active leaf and do not enter model context.
+
+The `ompgen2` discriminator prevents unsupported generation readers from opening submission-bearing data. Matched native copies retain origin facts and tombstones; a copied fact is inherited, never an admission into the destination. An unsupported required feature is refused. Product private admission remains blocked pending combined native/TUI/browser/fault acceptance.
+
+Public `HistoryItem.submission` carries only a validated original native origin and causal role. Retained entries are
+checked against their permanent reservation; running/live values come from the actual original object carrier. Copies
+retain the source origin. This is exact causal identity, while history remains observational and never substitutes for
+a committed submission receipt. Unknown native fields are omitted. Existing item/page/snapshot budgets and immutable
+cut checks include the new identity bytes. Native control rows are limited to8MiB each; later rows cannot forget earlier
+committed entry/no-entry facts, change causal roles or replace a known input outcome. Extension custom state cannot write
+the reserved `omp.native-control/` namespace. A refused native New operation preserves the current permanent ledger.
+
+`operationOutcome` is `succeeded`, `failed`, `cancelled` or `unknown`. It reports the primary native operation, separately from `inputOutcome`, relation persistence and terminal settlement. Only an actual local handler return or the exact native prompt ticket result supplies a known outcome. An acknowledgement, `agent_end`, `waitForIdle` or committed user entry alone cannot establish success; tool side effects may fail even when the primary operation succeeds. A restarted incomplete reservation and older records without this field report `unknown` unless a protected publication retained a known result. `no_input` means no initiating native input entry was generated: a successful handled operation can still append additional messages or perform effects.
+
+`submission_submit` accepts optional `idleOnly: true` for prompt input without a streaming hint. Native guards refuse busy or queued admission before input hooks, recheck protected authority after preprocessing awaits, and refuse a busy agent claim instead of waiting for an autonomous run. Ordinary callers retain their native queue and command behavior. Permanent duplicates are resolved before this new-admission check. A refused operation can retain a reservation and failed operation outcome; it must never be inferred to have succeeded from a no-input receipt.
+
+History item `submission` projects exact native origin and causal role for its entry identity, including running observations and copied origins. It never associates a local echo with a native row by text, order, or timestamps. Reserved `omp.native-control/` custom types are unavailable to extension appends. Persisted causal entries require a matching permanent reservation; later records cannot discard committed entry or no-entry facts.
